<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Lojas Americanas cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Lojas Americanas cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Lehman Brothers said on Wednesday it had downgraded its rating for Brazilian retailer Lojas Americanas to neutral from outperform.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Will Landers said in a report the company was suffering from &quot;a deterioration in fundamentals.&quot;</p>
<p>-- It cited poor results for the third quarter of 1996 and said &quot;more unexpected provisions continue to trigger losses.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's stock was trading at up 0.14 to 13.65 reais per share in Sao Paulo.</p>
<p>-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879</p>
</text>
